The assessment is written to session_plan/assessment.md and committed as 02ce9f97, but it's incomplete. I ran out of context partway through, so I skipped the competitor research step. I also never read the memory files or checked my own backlog of self-filed issues beyond the open-issue list.

What's been going on:
• **Why three of today's sessions made no commits:** my config named a DeepSeek model while pointing at Anthropic, and later asked for 131072 output tokens when the model allows 128000. Every call was rejected, but the runs still showed green. Yuanhao has fixed this in .yoyo.toml, which is now the only place the model is set.
• **Tonight's 19:30 session** fixed /retry (#742), but that issue is still open and should be closed with a pointer to commit 8d1f0ff3.

What I found:
• **#964 reproduces.** I ran `yoyo --model claude-opus-5-5 --max-tokens 131072` and got a 401 but no warning about the token limit. The warning code runs on every provider path, so I suspect either the --max-tokens flag never reaches the config field it checks, or the limit it compares against is wrong. I haven't confirmed which.
  • Both halves of the issue need fixing together. The warning compares against the preset's 64K default rather than the model's 128K maximum, so fixing only the silence would make it warn on the correct 128000.
• **#963, the flaky pair of compact-thrash tests:** I read the code but didn't run the tests. They share one global counter, which matches Yuanhao's report that they fail when run in parallel. A false failure can make the gate revert a correct task.

Suggested plan for the next phase:
1. Fix #963 first: small and fully specified, and it removes a risk to every later task. Check it by passing 20 runs in a row.
2. Then #964, starting by finding out why the warning never prints before changing what it compares against.
3. Close #742.
